      "rationale": "The single JSON envelope, always-object details, readable human mode, stderr diagnostics and raw-versus-JSON export channels are concrete and mutually consistent.",
      "source_citations": [
        {
          "section_id": ".specs/features/008-settings-cli/spec.md:L236-L240",
          "excerpt": "**Criterion:** With `--json`, stdout contains exactly one JSON envelope: success `{\"ok\": true, \"revision\": N, \"data\": …}`, failure `{\"ok\": false, \"error\": {\"code\": C, \"message\": M, \"details\": {…}}}` where `details` is always an object (for example `current_revision`, `outcome`, `field`, `issues` as a list of `{field, reason}`). Without `--json`, stdout shows readable text. Diagnostics, warnings and progress go to stderr in both modes. Export operations writing to `-` print only the exported content without `--json`, and put it in `data.content` of the envelope with `--json`."
        }
